WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 010, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.846
<v Gwen>Cardiff Times, thirtieth of December, eighteen sixty-four. Here she is, John bach: Amy, 'relict of the late Mr. John Williams, Great House farm.'

2
00:00:13.196 --> 00:00:21.273
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Great House farm. Tŷ Mawr, to us. Strange, seeing it in a Cardiff paper, in English, with her name beside it.

3
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:31.623
<v Gwen>Keep it. It shows she died a widow and the farm went by that name. It doesn't show who held the ground, or on what terms.

4
00:00:31.973 --> 00:00:38.127
<v Gwen>Eighteen sixty-six now. The new St Dochdwy's, consecrated, and half the Vale in their Sunday best.

5
00:00:38.477 --> 00:00:48.862
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>And the old church, put up around eighteen-twenty, taken down and carried off to Leckwith to stand again. Forty-odd years, and off it goes on a cart.

6
00:00:49.212 --> 00:00:55.365
<v Gwen>That's how a local-history blog tells it. None of us has held the consecration papers themselves.

7
00:00:59.715 --> 00:01:06.638
<v Gwen>Eighteen seventy-two, first of January: glebe land in this parish handed over as a site for a school.

8
00:01:06.988 --> 00:01:10.835
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Which glebe? The parson's fields run along half my hedges.

9
00:01:11.185 --> 00:01:21.954
<v Gwen>The deed's listed at Glamorgan Archives, P35CW/9. The catalogue line names glebe and a school site. It doesn't name the field, and we've not read the deed itself.

10
00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:28.842
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>Mr Williams? Assistant overseer, for the poor rate. Ninth of April. A moment of your time, please.

11
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:38.423
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>I have you entered as occupier of glebe land in Llandough. Owner: the Reverend H. H. Rickards. The rate falls on you as occupier.

12
00:01:38.773 --> 00:01:43.773
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>So I farm the church's field and pay the parish for the privilege.

13
00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:49.892
<v the assistant overseer of the poor>The book records who occupies and who owns, Mr Williams. That is all it records.

14
00:01:50.242 --> 00:02:03.319
<v Gwen>So it puts John on church glebe in eighteen seventy-two. Not which fields, nor that any Great House ground was his to own. And we've the entry, not yet the rate book's archive reference.

15
00:02:03.669 --> 00:02:09.823
<v John Williams of Great House Farm / Tŷ M>Glebe on one side, estate on the other, and Tŷ Mawr in the middle, paying both.

16
00:02:10.173 --> 00:02:15.942
<v Gwen>And down by the river they're talking lime and kilns. Paper's only getting thicker, John.
